\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. In all my vast concerns with Thee,
\par In vain my soul would try
\par To shun Thy presence, Lord, or flee
\par The notice of Thine eye.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy all-surrounding sight surveys
\par My rising and my rest,
\par My public walks, my private ways,
\par The secrets of my breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My thoughts lie open to Thee, Lord,
\par Before They're formed within;
\par And, ere my lips pronounce the word,
\par Thou know'st the sense I mean.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O wondrous knowledge, deep and high;
\par Where can a creature hide?
\par Within Thy circling arms I lie,
\par Beset on every side.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So let Thy grace surround me still,
\par And like a bulwark prove,
\par To guard my soul from every ill,
\par Secured by sovereign love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

